                <pb facs="0521" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/539: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >South</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-02T17:00:00-05:00">December 2, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>93. Minister for Foreign Affairs states Panaman Government will immediately take
                    the action indicated in penultimate sentence of your circular December 1, 5 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">4</hi>] p.m.</p>
                <closer>(Not signed)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
